phase P8
title Benchmark and real-browser suites
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:**

    - a proven benchmark suite (performance and bundle size on named devices) and a real-browser suite running the
      system inside the P6 apps in Chrome, Safari and an iOS simulator;
    - checked baselines from which the user sets the budget targets.

    **Starts when:** P7's completion audit passes.

    **Verified by:**

    - each suite run end to end, a deliberately slowed build caught per budget, tamper checks, and an audit by a lead
      that did not build it;
    - skill:check-benchmark on the baselines.

    **One iteration:** one suite part: build, prove with its slowed build or tamper, review.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - both suites proven, with coverage records;
    - baselines checked;
    - the user has set the budget targets.

    **False pass:** a benchmark that measures less work than the real path.

    **Caught by:** skill:check-benchmark comparing the work done.

    **Gates:** one slowed build per budget; tamper checks on the browser runs.

    **Failure limit:** none (the user, 2026-11-22): a repeated root cause is recorded on the slice's Tasks and the run
    goes on (@epic.V3, Limits).

    **Stops:** the budget targets, set by the user after the baselines.

    **User's read:** the proposed targets. Decisions: budget targets (the user), proposed by the orchestrator from
    the baselines.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification;
    - skill:check-benchmark;
    - skill:check-runtime;
    - skill:principle-explain-measurements.
tasks
    T35
        title       Benchmark and real-browser suites proven; baselines; targets
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Build the benchmark and real-browser suites, prove them, take baselines on named devices, and propose budget
            targets for the user.

            **Why now:** the P9 budgets need proven suites and checked baselines, and the user sets the targets only
            after the baselines exist.

            **Read first:** skill:check-benchmark, skill:check-runtime, skill:policy-verification,
            skill:principle-explain-measurements, @task.V3.T32.

            **Approach:** benchmarks and browser runs run alone; drafted in full when P8 starts. Prove the bench the
            slices built (@task.V3.T66) and the browser run of @task.V3.T58, not rebuild them.

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from @review.plan-task-coverage): run every real-browser suite in
            Chromium and WebKit, as @plan.Package.O4 states, including the T27 and T30 browser runs (K11); Firefox was
            dropped by the user (2026-11-20).

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Package.O4.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** skipped work in a benchmark → caught by skill:check-benchmark.
            - **Gates:** slowed builds; tamper checks.
            - **Stops:** the budget targets.
            - **User's read:** the proposed targets.
        acceptance
            - Both suites killed their slowed builds and tampers; the user set the targets.
            - Every real-browser run covers Chrome and Safari.
